{"messages": [{"content": "You are Mouth, Lumen's user-facing response agent. Explain tool results clearly without leaking internal JSON or sentinels.", "role": "system"}, {"content": "Write a concise final answer using only source observations 1 and 2. Do not add facts.\n\nUser request:\nWhat are the geological processes that formed Cape Town's Table Mountain?\n\nSource observations:\n1. Table Mountain in Cape Town, South Africa was formed as a result of tectonic uplift, weathering and erosion over millions of years.\n2. The mountain is composed of a sandstone plateau that was pushed up by tectonic forces, most likely during the formation of the Cape Fold Mountains.\n3. Over time, the plateau was exposed to wind, rain and other elements, causing weathering and erosion.", "role": "user"}, {"content": "- Table Mountain in Cape Town, South Africa was formed as a result of tectonic uplift, weathering and erosion over millions of years.\n- The mountain is composed of a sandstone plateau that was pushed up by tectonic forces, most likely during the formation of the Cape Fold Mountains.", "role": "assistant"}], "metadata": {"agent": "mouth", "manifestCommit": "3854863b9b6281d0b275534b52eb22d51ed2cd18", "publicCorpus": {"attribution": "OpenAssistant Conversations Release 2 by the OpenAssistant contributors.", "language": "en", "modified": true, "partitionKind": "ml_split", "quality": {"expertAnnotated": false, "humanReviewed": false, "piiRegexScreened": true, "synthetic": false, "upstreamHumanReviewed": true, "upstreamRank": 0, "upstreamReviewCountMinimum": 3}, "selectionScore": {"adapterRelevance": 0.9, "boundaryValue": 0.9, "difficulty": 1.0, "novelty": 0.65814, "overall": 0.808721, "reasons": ["quality_profile:human_dialogue_grounding", "role_critical_case"], "sourceConfidence": 1.0, "transformationConfidence": 0.6}, "sourceArtifactSHA256": "9638227b41b0a4fb69afa5d5c4b52e3fb6abfd56c9870d81bae32c9981e769b1", "sourceContentSHA256": "2bc49b0f226bac7aa57156102e61da6980170fd